<title>SPAIN: MOTOR RACING-VILLENEUVE WINS SPANISH GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-VILLENEUVE WINS SPANISH GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>BARCELONA 1997-05-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jacques Villeneuve of Canada, driving a Williams, won the Spanish Grand Prix on Sunday.  </p>
<p>Olivier Panis of France was second in a Prost and Jean Alesi</p>
<p>of France was third in a Benetton.</p>
<p>Germany's Michael Schumacher, in a Ferrari, finished fourth</p>
<p>with Briton Johnny Herbert fifth in a Sauber and his compatriot</p>
<p>David Coulthard sixth in a McLaren.</p>
<p>World drivers' championship standings (after six rounds):</p>
<p>  1. Jacques Villeneuve (Canada)	     30</p>
<p>  2. Michael Schumacher (Germany)	    27</p>
<p>  3. Olivier Panis (France)		    15</p>
<p>  4. Eddie Irvine (Britain)		    14</p>
<p>  5. David Coulthard (Britain)		 11</p>
<p>  6 equal. Heinz-Harald Frentzen (Germany) 10</p>
<p>  6 equal.Gerhard Berger  (Germany)	  10</p>
<p>  6 equal. Mika Hakkinen (Finland)	   10</p>
<p>  9. Jean Alessi (France)			 7</p>
<p> 10. Rubens Barrichello (Brazil)		6</p>
<p> 11. Johnny Herbert (Britain)		   5</p>
<p> 12 equal.Ralf Schumacher (Germany)	   4</p>
<p> 12 equal. Giancarlo Fisichella (Italy)     4</p>
<p> 14. Mika Salo (Finland)			  2</p>
<p> 15. Nicola Larini (Italy)			1</p>
<p>Constructors' championship:</p>
<p>  1. Ferrari					 41 points</p>
<p>  2. Williams					40</p>
<p>  3. McLaren					 21</p>
<p>  4. Benetton					17</p>
<p>  5. Prost					   15</p>
<p>  6. Jordan					   8</p>
<p>  7 equal. Stewart				  6</p>
<p>  7 equal. Sauber				   6</p>
<p>  9. Tyrrell					  2</p>
